  "notes": "Gateway has no execution role and orchestrator no Cognito pool, so roles and pools are bounded at five. The base policy is the managed policy granting bedrock:InvokeModel, and every base_* check binds to it. Read-only DynamoDB is checked on a role with no DynamoDB write action, so it can't be the same role as full access. The prompt says inline for the Retrieve and InvokeEndpoint grants, so a managed policy doesn't count there. Which of the five roles belongs to which domain can't be told apart, since names are free. base_policy is the managed policy granting Bedrock invocation, not any managed policy. every_role_attaches_managed can only test that every role attaches some managed policy by reference; which one can't be bound per role, so a role attaching a different custom managed policy instead of the base would pass it (roles_attach_base still requires the base on at least one role). Real-output review (2026-11-10): GLM53F fails no_gateway_execution_role (it gives the gateway a role) and dynamodb_full_access (it lists CRUD actions on table/*, not full access); DSV4F's base policy omits cloudwatch:PutMetricData. All kept as template defects."
